course: dictionary
lesson: 9857
title: Sympathetic: understanding and caring
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Her sympathetic friend sat with her until the tears stopped.» Sympathetic means showing that you understand and care about someone's sadness or problems. The clues are sat with her and the tears stopped: she listened and helped. Try your meaning in the sentence: a caring, understanding friend fits, so you know it is right.
explain: Sympathetic can also mean agreeing with an idea or supporting a group. «The mayor was sympathetic to the plan for a new park.» He was not sad for anyone here. Clue: he wanted the park to be built, so he was on the side of the plan.
explain: In a story, a sympathetic character is one readers like and care about. «Poor Ben was lost in the storm, and he kept helping his little sister anyway.» Authors make characters sympathetic by showing their struggles and their kindness. Ask yourself: who do I feel sorry for, and who do I want to win?
fact: Sympathetic is an adjective: sympathetic, more sympathetic, most sympathetic.
fact: «Sympathetic» means showing that you understand and care about someone's sadness or problems.
fact: Listening, saying kind words and helping when a friend is upset are all sympathetic things to do.
fact: The sitar has «sympathetic strings» that are not plucked but vibrate by themselves when matching notes are played.
fact: Ravi Shankar made the sitar famous worldwide, and George Harrison of the Beatles learned from him.
exercise: «Her sympathetic friend sat with her until she stopped crying.» What does sympathetic mean here? | Very tired and sleepy | Loud and bossy | Angry with everyone | *Caring and understanding about someone's sadness
exercise: The mayor was «sympathetic to the plan» for a new park. What does this mean? | He argued against it loudly | He did not know about it | He forgot it completely | *He agreed with it and supported it
exercise: Which character would be a sympathetic character in a story? | A character who has no feelings at all | A character who is never mentioned | *A character readers like and care about, who shows kindness and struggles | A character who is always rude and never says sorry
test: «The nurse was sympathetic when I told her about my sore knee.» What does sympathetic mean? | Bored by my story | Happy to hear about my knee | *Understanding and caring about my pain | Very cold and distant
test: What is the best way to show you are sympathetic to a friend who is upset? | Laugh at their problem | Tell everyone about it | *Listen and say kind words | Ignore them and walk away
exam: Which sentence shows someone being sympathetic? | «She ran off without a single word.» | «She counted the coins twice.» | «She painted the fence blue.» | *«She hugged her crying cousin and asked if he was okay.»
